# Technical Stack
tech_stack:
  framework: spring-boot
  build_tool: Gradle
  java_version: 21
  database: postgres
  cache: aerospike
  message_queue: kafka
  monitoring: prometheus
  logging: logback
  testing: junit
  security: spring-security


# Overall Guidelines
* Use lombok only for dto
* for api requests use `src/main/java/com/ttn/common/util/AppUtil.java`
* for s3 related tasks look for `src/main/java/com/ttn/common/util/S3Util.java`
* for spring security related methods look for `src/main/java/com/ttn/common/util/SecurityUtil.java`
* Spring Security configurations are in `src/main/java/com/ttn/common/config/CommonConfiguration.java` and `src/main/java/com/ttn/common/config/CommonBlockingConfiguration.java`
* for any utility related methods search for `src/main/java/com/ttn/common/util/Util.java`
* For Exception, use `src/main/java/com/ttn/common/exception/TTNException.java`, e.g use something like 
    throw new TTNException(ErrorCode.CANNOT_MODIFY); 
    where ErrorCode file exists at path `src/main/java/com/ttn/common/enums/ErrorCode`
* Check for `build.gradle` for dependencies
* Check for `application.yml` for properties
* Use `config/TTNConfig.java` as ConfigurationProperties   
* Don't write methods more than 50 lines try to modularize it
* Do not write business logic in controller, always write in service class
